1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:03,000
Exhaust smoke color
is a clue.

2
00:00:03,000 --> 00:00:07,000
Blue-gray smoke usually points
to oil getting into the engine

3
00:00:07,000 --> 00:00:11,000
and burning off — often worn
valve seals or piston rings.

4
00:00:11,000 --> 00:00:15,000
Thick white smoke that doesn't
clear after warm-up

5
00:00:15,000 --> 00:00:19,000
can point to coolant getting
into the engine — that one shouldn't wait.

6
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:23,000
Black smoke usually means
the engine's running rich,

7
00:00:23,000 --> 00:00:27,000
burning more fuel than it
should — worth checking, not a guess.

8
00:00:27,000 --> 00:00:30,000
Stop by and we'll take a look.
Nick's Tire & Auto
